  "report_period": "Week 31 (24th Jul to 31st Jul 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Attikos\" 179/2012 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 01/2027, Scrubber fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 37,5 mill. By way of comparison, the two-years-older sister vessel \"Nicholas G.S\" 179/2010 Sungdong, Korea (SS 07/2030, DD 02/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold a week ago at UD 34,5 mill. Japanese owners have committed the Kamsarmax \"Mont Fort\" 82/2012 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 02/2027, Scrubber fitted) to Greek interests at USD 22 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Key Hunter\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 12/2027) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 20,9 mill. The Panamax \"G. B. Corrado\" 77/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 03/2028) of Gestion Maritime was committed to Korean interests at USD 15 mill. For reference, the \"Alexandros Petrakis\" 76/2008 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) was sold back in April at USD 13,3 mill. Keiyo Kisen have committed their Ultramax \"CMB Jordaens\" 63/2019 Tadotsu, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 08/2027) at USD 35,5 mill. Note that earlier this month, the one-year-younger \"WF Artemis\" 63/2020 Iwagi, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD 05/2028) was sold at USD 36,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Atlantides Shipping committed their \"Agios Nektarios I\" 56/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 08/2030, DD 11/2028) at USD 13,3 mill. By way of comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Omega S\" 56/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 08/2026) was sold a month ago at low USD 14 mill. In addition, Liannex Corporation committed the \"Lianson Hermes\" 53/2009 Zhejiang, China (SS 04/2029, DD 06/2027) at USD 13 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Xing Ning He\" 53/2009 Zhejiang, China (SS 01/2029, DD 12/2026) was sold back in May at USD 11 mill. Shunzan Kaiun committed their Handysize \"Sakura Dream\" 38/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 12/2030, DD 12/2028) at USD 18,5 mill basis delivery Nov- Dec'26, while MUR Shipping committed the one-year-younger sister vessel \"African Harrier\" 37/2014 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2029, DD 08/2027) at USD 20,1 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the sister vessel \"Astro Propus\" 38/2014 Imabari, Japan (SS 05/2029, DD 08/2027) was sold at USD 19 mill.",
    "tankers": "Western Shipping committed the LR2 \"Ellie Lady\" 110/2009 Sungdong, Korea (SS 10/2029, DD 11/2027, Scrubber fitted) to clients of Trafigura at USD 47,5 mill. For reference, the \"Jag Lokesh\" 105/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS 01/2029, DD 10/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 44 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route showed a firmer tone, with Port Hedland and Dampier to Qingdao fixtures settling between USD 11.15/12.50 fio. In the Atlantic, Tubarao and Itaguai departures to Qingdao, including West Africa options, secured between USD 32.10/33.75 fio, while a long-haul run from Port Cartier achieved USD 46.70 fio. Out of South Africa, a Saldanha Bay trip to Qingdao fetched USD 24.12 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, Australian rounds with redelivery in China, South Korea, India and South East Asia fetched between USD 11,750/19,000 pd, alongside a long-haul trip from Continent via Australia to South Korea fixing at USD 34,400 pd. NoPac trips with Singapore/Japan, Far East and India options settled between USD 14,750/18,250 pd. Indonesian coal runs to China, India, Japan and local ranges achieved USD 11,100/18,000 pd, while a North China trip to South East Asia made USD 10,000 pd. From East Coast India, West Coast India and South East Asia, trips via ECSA and South Africa to India and Far East destinations obtained USD 16,000/21,000 pd and USD 19,000 pd respectively. In the Atlantic, Continent trips via USEC to India and South East Asia reached between USD 33,000/34,000 pd, while an intra-Continent run via Narvik made USD 22,000 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, trips from North China via Indonesia to East Coast India fixed at USD 18,000 pd, while a run to the Persian Gulf achieved USD 25,500 pd and a trip from Singapore to China settled at USD 15,500 pd. From East Australia, a trip to South East Asia fetched USD 22,000 pd plus USD 345,000 ballast bonus. Out of India, coastal and local round trips, including runs via South East Asia, settled between USD 17,750/20,000 pd. In the Atlantic, transatlantic runs from NCSA and ECSA to the Continent obtained between USD 16,000/25,000 pd. Out of South Africa, coal trips to West Coast India, Pakistan and Japan ranges secured between USD 22,000/27,000 pd alongside ballast bonuses ranging from USD 220,000 to USD 270,000.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Activity in the Handysize segment remained subdued for another week, with limited fixtures reported. In the Atlantic, an alumina run from the Caribbean to Continent fixed at USD 16,500 pd, while a NCSA trip to ECSA range fetched USD 15,200 pd. Out of Continent, a transatlantic grain run to NCSA settled at USD 9,500 pd, whereas a West Med trip via Safi to West Africa achieved USD 15,500 pd."
    }
  },
